Non-commercial means not primarily intended for or directed toward
commercial advantage or monetary compensation. Teaching, preaching, private
study, scholarship, parish use, and free public reference works are all
clearly within it.

Full license text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/


4. COMMERCIAL USE — ASK

Commercial use of the LICENSED MATERIAL requires written permission. This
includes print or ebook editions made from these files, subscription or
paywalled databases, and inclusion in commercial software or reference
products.

This restriction does not reach the 1825 text itself. Set Milton's Latin or
Sumner's English from the public-domain source and sell it; nothing here
restrains you.

Permission is not hard to get, and is given readily for scholarly and
ecclesial projects. Write to wilson@wrootlabs.com.

The copyright holder retains all rights and is not bound by this license;
Wroot Press publishes print editions drawn from this material.


5. STATUS

This edition is a working draft. Book II is complete; Book I is in progress.
Citations whose divergence has not been checked against the
Junius–Tremellius Bible are marked as unchecked on the site, and that mark
means what it says. Cite this as a draft, and check back for revisions.


6. SUGGESTED ATTRIBUTION

  Parallel edition, citation index, and notes to Milton's De Doctrina
